# deploy/compose/log-redact.caddy
#
# Installed at /home/puni1/wbs/caddy/log-redact.caddy by configure.sh and
# imported by the host Caddyfile before any site file. Every rendered
# site.caddy (tools/tool-compose/src/templates/site.caddy.tmpl) and every
# hand-maintained vhost does `import access-log` instead of defining a log
# block, so this file is the ONLY place the access log is configured.
#
# The single access-log definition. Every vhost that logs imports this snippet
# instead of writing its own `log { output file … }` block, because all of them
# write to the SAME file and a leak needs only one of them to opt out.
#
# Why the filter exists (queue TASK-159, 2026-08-26). Caddy logs `request.uri`
# verbatim, query string included, and that file is durable: 49 MB live, five
# rotated .gz siblings back to 2026-08-04, and it is the input to
# /home/puni1/monitoring/bin/goaccess-reports.sh, which copies whatever it finds
# into generated HTML under /home/puni1/monitoring/www. Two credential-shaped
# values were landing there:
#
#   * `code`/`state` on /api/auth/okta/callback — 13 occurrences. Single-use,
#     PKCE-protected, so not a live takeover path.
#   * `token` on dev.wbs.bulletpoints.club/ws — 10,901 occurrences, 16 distinct
#     HS256 JWTs with a 12-hour lifetime. THIS is the one that mattered: for
#     twelve hours after each line is written, that log holds a replayable
#     session credential.
#
# `replace` rather than `hash`: GoAccess counts URLs, and collapsing every
# tokened request to one URI makes the report more readable, not less. Params
# not present in a request are left alone, so listing extras costs nothing.
#
# Verified before it shipped: a throwaway caddy:2-alpine on :8099 logged
# `code=REDACTED&keep=visible&state=REDACTED` with this filter and
# `code=SECRETCODE123` without it. The negative control is the point — the
# filter is known to fail loudly, not merely to look present.
(access-log) {
	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/access.log
		format filter {
			wrap json
			fields {
				request>uri query {
					replace code REDACTED
					replace state REDACTED
					replace token REDACTED
					replace access_token REDACTED
					replace id_token REDACTED
					replace refresh_token REDACTED
					replace session REDACTED
					replace password REDACTED
					replace secret REDACTED
					replace api_key REDACTED
					replace apikey REDACTED
					replace signature REDACTED
					replace sig REDACTED
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
